  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets duri...\n- {\"content\":\"To find the percentage of sales from sunflower bouquets:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{12}{50}\\\\times 100\\\\% = 24\\\\%\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{24\\\\%}\\n\\\\]\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Faraday owns a flower shop.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The correction from “flower stall” to “flower shop” does not change the numbers:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\% = 24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many sunflower bouquets did Faraday sell per day on average during that week? Additionally, Faraday's flower shop was open for 6 days during that week.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets over 6 days. The average per day was:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{6}=2\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ sunflower bouquets per day}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $3 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Noted: individual sunflowers cost \\$3 each. This does not change the average of \\(\\boxed{2}\\) sunflower bouquets sold per day. A revenue calculation would require knowing how many individual sunflowers Faraday sold.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day from individual sunflowers and $56 per day from bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Individual sunflowers cost \\$3 each, and Faraday earns \\$26 per day from selling them.\n\nOver 3 days, he earns:\n\n\\[\n26 \\times 3 = \\$78\n\\]\n\nThe number of individual sunflowers sold is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{78}{3}=26\n\\]\n\nThe bouquet information is not needed because the number of sunflowers in each bouquet is unspecified.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{26\\text{ individual sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Over 3 days:\n\n- Individual sunflowers:  \n  \\[\n  \\$26 \\times 3=\\$78,\\qquad \\$78\\div \\$3=26\n  \\]\n  So, 26 individual sunflowers.\n\n- Bouquets:  \n  \\[\n  \\$56\\div \\$8=7\\text{ bouquets per day}\n  \\]\n  Over 3 days:\n  \\[\n  7\\times3=21\\text{ bouquets}\n  \\]\n  Since each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers:\n  \\[\n  21\\times12=252\\text{ sunflowers}\n  \\]\n\nTotal sunflowers:\n\n\\[\n26+252=\\boxed{278\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With individual sunflowers priced at \\$2 each:\n\n- Individual sunflowers sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$26\\times 3}{\\$2}=\\frac{78}{2}=39\n  \\]\n\n- Bouquets sold in 3 days:\n  \\[\n  \\frac{\\$56}{\\$8}\\times 3=7\\times3=21\n  \\]\n\n- Sunflowers in bouquets:\n  \\[\n  21\\times12=252\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of sunflowers sold was:\n\n\\[\n39+252=\\boxed{291\\text{ sunflowers}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
